Two changes to isla-footprint of Isla e9b5d945 (https://github.com/rems-project/isla), which
tests/isla/traces.sh uses to trace the A64 model's loads and stores.  Without the two new options
the patched Isla runs as the original: Memory::read returns to its old code at once when memory
holds no fixed entry, and the lookup of reset constraints consults the instruction's fields only
under the new flag.  Apply with `patch -p1` in a copy of the e9b5d945 tree.

--fixed-memory EXPRESSION=VALUE.  The reset builtin evaluates EXPRESSION, an SMT expression over
registers, after it asserts the reset constraints and with their lookup, and fixes the bytes of
VALUE, 1 to 8 of them, at the resulting address in the frame's memory, which every path inherits.
Memory::read answers an untagged read of that many bytes with VALUE when Z3 proves the read's
address equal to the entry's, fails with Z3Unknown when Z3 cannot decide, and otherwise reads as
before.  An answered read records a read-mem event with VALUE at the address that the
specification passed, so a checker of the trace verifies that memory holds VALUE at the address
that the translation table walk computed.  The change adds no assertion to the solver and changes
no write.  It lets TTBR0_EL1 stay symbolic while the walk reads the startup's descriptors, which no
stock mechanism provides: --armv8-page-tables places tables at concrete addresses only, and a read
from symbolic memory returns a fresh value whose fields fork the walk without bound.

--reset-constraint-fields.  With this flag, a name in a --reset-constraint that names a field of
the --partial instruction denotes the field's variable.  The lookup consults the fields before the
symbol table, which also holds the IR's local variables, among them names such as imm12, and it
fails on a name that is both a field and a register.  Isla records the constraint as an assume
event and asserts it, as it does any reset constraint, so a theorem over the trace carries it as a
premise.  The flag lets one constraint relate a base register to an immediate, such as
X[Rn] + 8 * imm12 lying in the RAM GiB.

isla-lib/src/memory.rs holds the entries and the test in Memory::read, isla-lib/src/executor.rs
the lookup and the evaluation of the entries at reset, isla-lib/src/executor/task.rs the entries
and the field variables that TaskState carries, and src/footprint.rs the options and the field
variables that instruction_to_val returns.

